# The Vulkan loader used by the pinned Linux wgpu-native runtime retains one
# process-global physical-device enumeration allocation plus two 56-byte
# worker/TLS records after a child engine renders a nested picture mask.
# ProGPU releases both engines and all WebGPU handles. The pinned ash helper is
# symbolized; the stripped Mesa/Vulkan worker frames are reported only as
# `<unknown module>`. ProGPU/ASan frames remain symbolized, so this second rule
# does not suppress leaks rooted entirely in ProGPU code.
leak:ash::prelude::read_into_uninitialized_vector
leak:<unknown module>
